## KEY INSIGHT: Assembly Analysis

Analyzed generated assembly for claude7_1 and discovered:
- Inner loops call malloc/free for EVERY promoted panel!
- A panel: 192×192×8 = 294,912 bytes → malloc in hot K loop (4 calls)
- B panel: 192×48×8 = 73,728 bytes → malloc in hot N loop (32 calls)
- Both exceed default max-alloc-size-in-bytes=65536
- These heap allocations should be stack allocations!

