## New Session - Round 10+ (claude21+): Novel Techniques Research

Researched new MLIR transform operations not yet tried:
- transform.structured.pad + hoist_pad: Pad tiles to fixed sizes, eliminate remainder
- transform.structured.interchange: Reorder iterators for better access patterns
- transform.structured.fuse: Fuse fill into tiled matmul
- transform.structured.pack: Data layout transformation for cache efficiency
- pad_tiling_interface: Pad dimensions to multiples for cleaner vectorization
- Different split_transfer strategies
- Affine loop approach (convert-linalg-to-affine-loops) with polyhedral optimizations

Strategy: Focus on techniques fundamentally different from BLIS tiling already explored.

## KEY INSIGHT: Assembly Analysis (Session 2)

Analyzed assembly of claude13_1 and discovered that malloc/free calls are STILL present
despite promote-buffers-to-stack{max-alloc-size-in-bytes=524288}. The promoted allocs
are inside scf.forall (parallel region) and promote-buffers-to-stack does NOT convert
allocations inside parallel regions to stack allocations.

This means the 2.11x→2.02x improvement from claude7→claude13 was NOT from eliminating
malloc (it's still there!) but from other pipeline changes (extra canonicalize/cse passes).

