## Session 7: K_inner=8 Hybrid Micro-Kernel (claude71-claude86)
=============================================================

### K_inner=8 Breakthrough
Instead of BLIS K=1 + K-unroll=8 (which generated 96 redundant C stores per micro-tile
because transfer_to_scf lowering doesn't keep accumulators register-resident across
loop iterations), using tile_sizes [6, 8, 8] (K_inner=8) lets the vectorizer see a
6×8×8 contraction where accumulators stay register-resident across all 8 K-steps.
Combined with K_outer unroll=4, this produces 48 C stores per 32 K-values (1.5/K-value)
vs old 96 per 8 K-values (12/K-value) — an 8x reduction in C memory traffic.

