Key insight: Intermediate C stores are ~47% overhead (56 stores / 120 total memory ops).
The performance gap (3.39x vs MKL) is too large for micro-kernel tuning alone.
Likely dominated by:
1. memrefCopy overhead for promotion (2 calls per K×N tile)
2. Suboptimal data layout (promoted panels contiguous but not physically repacked)
3. No software prefetching (MKL uses explicit prefetch instructions)

