  * K_inner=16 no unroll — neutral (eliminates store/reload but doesn't improve overall)
  * Different micro-kernel shape (2×16) — worse
  * enable-x86vector flag — neutral
  * Extra optimization passes (LISH, LICM) — neutral
- Key findings:
  * C store/reload between K-blocks is caused by LLVM alias analysis (C in %arg2 may alias A/B alloca)
  * Cannot fix without either: (a) LLVM noalias hints, or (b) external micro-kernel library
  * C promotion eliminates alias but adds copy overhead that outweighs the benefit
  * hoist_redundant_vector_transfers only works on vector.transfer_read/write, not vector.load/store

