=== SESSION 32 SUMMARY ===
Tested 47 variants (claude377-423)

*** MAJOR BREAKTHROUGH: KC=512 (Full K) ***
Best: claude415_2 = 1.74x (stable ~1.75x), vs previous 2.03x = 14% improvement
Key insight: With KC=512 (entire K dimension), there is only ONE K-loop iteration,
which completely eliminates the C alias store/reload problem between K-blocks!
This was the #1 bottleneck identified in sessions 28-31.

Optimal KC=512 configuration:
- 64×64 forall (8x8 = 64 tasks for 28 cores)
- KC=512 (full K dimension, single iteration)
- promA at K-level: A panel 64×512 = 256KB alloca
- NC=16 + promB at inner N-level: B panel 512×16 = 64KB alloca
- 4×8×8 micro-kernel (K_inner=8)
- K unroll=4
- Inline copy (no linalg_copy_to_memref)

Why KC=512 works but didn't work in session 31 (claude370 at 2.13x):
- Session 31 used 128×128 forall → A panel was 128×512 = 512KB (L2 thrash!)
- Session 32 uses 64×64 forall → A panel is 64×512 = 256KB (fits in L2)

matmul_1 unchanged: 1.44x (claude154) — no improvement from any session 32 approach

